{"company":{"id":"spotify","name":"Spotify","accent":"#1db954","asset":"audio frames","verb":"play"},"nodes":[{"id":"client","title":"App / TV / web","kind":"client","blurb":"Starts play, browse, and account calls.","depth":0,"story":"This is the Spotify app on your phone or laptop. Tapping play starts here. The app does not hold the whole product — it only starts the request."},{"id":"dns","title":"DNS","kind":"api","blurb":"Finds the nearest edge for this user.","depth":0,"story":"Your phone asks “where is the nearest Spotify door?” DNS points at a close edge so the first hop is short."},{"id":"cdn","title":"CDN / Open Connect","kind":"cdn","blurb":"Holds hot video segments close to the viewer.","depth":1,"story":"On Spotify, bulky audio frames are copied around the world. Play/browse should hit a nearby copy. If that copy is missing, a miss goes back to origin."},{"id":"api","title":"API gateway","kind":"api","blurb":"Auth, routing, rate limits for control-plane calls.","depth":1,"story":"Think of this as Spotify’s front desk. The app asks it for “what’s allowed / what’s next,” not for huge audio frames. It routes, limits traffic, and hides internal stores."},{"id":"auth","title":"Identity","kind":"auth","blurb":"Who is watching, which profile, which plan.","depth":2,"story":"Before Spotify shows anything private, it checks who you are (account, session, device). A CDN copy of a file is not the same as being logged in."},{"id":"playback","title":"Playback service","kind":"service","blurb":"Manifests, licenses, bitrate ladders — how this play is allowed to start.","depth":2,"story":"Playback on Spotify is “which file, which quality, am I allowed?” — not “dump the whole movie from a database.”"},{"id":"catalog","title":"Catalog service","kind":"service","blurb":"Titles, seasons, availability by country and device.","depth":2,"story":"The list of what exists (titles, seasons, regions). It is metadata, not the video bytes you watch."},{"id":"drm","title":"License / DRM","kind":"auth","blurb":"This device may decrypt this title for this window of time.","depth":2,"story":"Even after audio frames arrive, Spotify checks a license: this device, this title, this window of time. Stops a stolen file from playing everywhere."},{"id":"recs","title":"Recommendations","kind":"service","blurb":"Ranks “what to watch next” from history and catalog signals.","depth":3,"story":"The “because you watched…” row is scored from your history and the catalog. Your phone does not download the whole library to rank it."},{"id":"cfg","title":"Config / experiments","kind":"service","blurb":"Which homepage layout and bitrate caps this user gets.","depth":3,"story":"Spotify can show two homepages to two similar users (experiments). That config is a service, not a one-off if-statement in the app."},{"id":"cache","title":"Hot cache","kind":"cache","blurb":"Session, title rows, and continue-watching that everyone hammers.","depth":3,"story":"The same questions get asked thousands of times (session, “is this still available?”). Spotify keeps those answers in fast memory so the main database is not hit every time."},{"id":"userdb","title":"User / history DB","kind":"db","blurb":"Profiles, continue-watching, my-list.","depth":4,"story":"Your continue-watching / saved list lives here. It is tiny compared with audio frames, and it is queried often."},{"id":"metadb","title":"Metadata DB","kind":"db","blurb":"Canonical title graph, not the video bytes.","depth":4,"story":"The official map of titles and relationships. Separate from your personal history and from the video warehouse."},{"id":"blob","title":"Object store","kind":"blob","blurb":"Mezzanine + packaged segments.","depth":4,"story":"The warehouse for large audio frames. Cheap to store, not great for “show my last 20 items.” Spotify points at these files from the records database."},{"id":"queue","title":"Encode queue","kind":"queue","blurb":"New titles and extra bitrates wait here.","depth":5,"story":"Slow leftover work (encode, notify, payout) waits here after you already succeeded at play. The tap can return; workers finish later."},{"id":"encoder","title":"Transcoders","kind":"workers","blurb":"Many resolutions/codecs off the request path.","depth":5,"story":"Spotify does not wait while you tap play to create every quality. Extra sizes and formats are cooked in the background from a master file."},{"id":"origin","title":"Origin / packager","kind":"blob","blurb":"Fills the CDN on cache miss.","depth":5,"story":"Only used when the nearby copy does not have that audio frames yet. Origin fetches from the warehouse and restocks the CDN — it should not be on every Play."},{"id":"notify","title":"Messaging","kind":"workers","blurb":"“New episode” and device sync.","depth":6,"story":"“New episode” or “your driver is here” is a background ping. It is not part of the Play / tap request that already succeeded."},{"id":"abr","title":"Bitrate / ABR","kind":"service","blurb":"Picks a quality as the network changes.","depth":2,"story":"As your wifi changes, Spotify switches audio frames quality. That decision is not “one giant file or nothing.”"},{"id":"telemetry","title":"Play quality logs","kind":"queue","blurb":"Stalls and bitrate — after play, not on the Play tap.","depth":6,"story":"Spotify logs stalls and quality after play. That telemetry is a background stream, not the Play path itself."},{"id":"playlist-sync","title":"Playlist sync","kind":"service","blurb":"Keeps playlist edits ordered across phones, desktop, and offline devices.","depth":6,"story":"Keeps playlist edits ordered across phones, desktop, and offline devices."}],"edges":[{"from":"client","to":"dns","label":"find nearest"},{"from":"client","to":"cdn","label":"video bytes"},{"from":"client","to":"api","label":"play / browse"},{"from":"dns","to":"cdn","label":"point to edge"},{"from":"api","to":"auth","label":"who is this"},{"from":"api","to":"playback","label":"start stream"},{"from":"api","to":"catalog","label":"what exists"},{"from":"playback","to":"drm","label":"license"},{"from":"api","to":"cfg","label":"which experiment"},{"from":"playback","to":"cdn","label":"fetch segments"},{"from":"catalog","to":"cache","label":"hot titles"},{"from":"catalog","to":"metadb","label":"title graph"},{"from":"recs","to":"cache","label":"rank features"},{"from":"recs","to":"userdb","label":"watch history"},{"from":"playback","to":"userdb","label":"continue watching"},{"from":"cdn","to":"origin","label":"cache miss"},{"from":"origin","to":"blob","label":"source files"},{"from":"queue","to":"encoder","label":"new title"},{"from":"encoder","to":"blob","label":"packaged output"},{"from":"catalog","to":"queue","label":"publish job"},{"from":"notify","to":"userdb","label":"who to ping"},{"from":"playback","to":"abr","label":"which quality"},{"from":"playback","to":"telemetry","label":"quality after play"},{"from":"workers","to":"playlist-sync","label":"sync libraries"}],"stages":[{"i":0,"blurb":"Two roads already: the app talks to an API for “what to play,” and video files come from a nearby copy (CDN)—not from a far-away warehouse first.","unlockNodeIds":["client","dns","cdn","api"],"unlockEdgeIds":["client->dns","client->cdn","client->api","dns->cdn","api->auth","api->playback","api->catalog","api->cfg","playback->cdn","cdn->origin"]},{"i":1,"blurb":"Next: who you are, which title, start playback, a license, and which quality. Play is several services, not one video database.","unlockNodeIds":["auth","playback","catalog","drm","abr"],"unlockEdgeIds":["api->auth","api->playback","api->catalog","playback->drm","playback->cdn","catalog->cache","catalog->metadb","playback->userdb","catalog->queue","playback->abr","playback->telemetry"]},{"i":2,"blurb":"The homepage is ranked for you. Frequent answers (titles, session) sit in a fast cache so the database is not hit every time.","unlockNodeIds":["recs","cfg","cache"],"unlockEdgeIds":["api->cfg","catalog->cache","recs->cache","recs->userdb"]},{